nintendo's latest direct was a wild ride  and we're talking all about that and  more  nintendo aired its first direct of 2022  and made a handful of fun announcements  for fans one of the biggest  announcements came in the form of a  booster course pack for mario kart 8  deluxe that will add 48 additional dlc  courses to the popular racing game by  the end of 2023 the first wave of  courses arrives on march 18th the dlc  will include remastered courses from  earlier games a-courses will be released  across six waves for a total of 48  courses in all some of the courses  confirmed so far include coconut mall  from mario kart wii cocoa mountain from  mario kart 64 and tokyo blur from mario  kart tour these will be available in the  first wave and they can be played  locally and online the booster course  pack costs 25 on its own but it's also  included in the nintendo switch online  plus expansion pass at no extra cost  along with that nintendo is finally  delivering us the sequel to one of the  wii's best games like his predecessor  switch sports delivers a bunch of  different sports to play all of which  are played with motion controls other  highlights from the direct include new  difficulty modes for metroid prime dread  a new co-op trailer for splatoon 3  earthbound and earthbound beginnings  coming to switch online as well as a  brand new mario strikers game nintendo  closed the show with the reveal of  xenoblade chronicles 3 a new trailer for  the upcoming jrpg showcase the game's  characters and tease the plot xenoblade  chronicles 3 is scheduled for launch in  september of 2022  according to multiple new reports a new  assassin's creed game focused on stealth  is coming either this year or next year  and will feature the assassin's creed  valhalla character basm bloomberg was  the first to report on the supposed  existence of this game which is  supposedly codenamed rift eurogamer's  own sources said that this is a real  project as well according to bloomberg's  report ubisoft originally conceived this  rumored project as an expansion for  valhalla however it's now allegedly  being prepared for release as a  standalone game rift or whatever the  game will end up being called if it's  the real deal will not feature the type  of gigantic open worlds that the  franchise is known for instead it will  be smaller in scope and focus on stealth  gameplay instead of the action rpg  nature of origins through valhalla this  possible project is separate from  ubisoft's ambitious new project  assassin's creed infinity which is  confirmed to be in development but still  doesn't have any concrete information  yet  a spokesperson for ubisoft sent a  statement to gamespot that said in part  quote we don't comment or engage on  rumors or speculation as they do a  disservice to our development teams and  community  sony has rolled out a new beta for its  ps4 and ps5 adding a suite of ui changes  adjustments and accessibility features  most notably though is an entirely new  feature coming to ps5 that will let  users give the console voice commands  limited to us and uk users players who  make it into the beta will be able to  have their ps5 open on a game or an app  as well as pause or resume media  playback using their voice just like ps4  users can the ps5's ui is also getting  some slight changes although folders a  popular feature on the ps4  aren't on that list instead users will  be able to filter their game collection  by genre and tag some to be kept on  their home screen additionally the home  screen will be able to hold a total of  14 games and apps according to the blog  post access will only be open to  selected beta participants in applicable  countries of course everyone with a ps5  or ps4 will be able to try out these new  features when they officially roll out  later this year assuming that they do so  what was your favorite part of the  nintendo direct let us know in the  comments below  you
 

